WEBVTT

1
00:00:33.500 --> 00:00:37.416


2
00:00:37.416 --> 00:00:41.625
<b>Son of Kunti, Arjuna's mind</b>
<b>is stuck on the thought</b>

3
00:00:41.625 --> 00:00:43.916
<b>that he will not be able to fight the war.</b>

4
00:00:43.916 --> 00:00:45.875
<b>He is a follower of dharma,</b>

5
00:00:45.875 --> 00:00:48.958
<b>and according to him, killing his own people</b>

6
00:00:48.958 --> 00:00:51.333
<b>is a grave sin, isn't it?</b>

7
00:00:52.000 --> 00:00:56.166


8
00:00:56.166 --> 00:01:00.375
<b>Arjuna just wants that somehow, all of this stops, </b>

9
00:01:00.375 --> 00:01:04.833
<b>and his hands do not get tainted with</b>
<b>anyone's blood in this war... </b>

10
00:01:04.833 --> 00:01:08.875
<b>The internal conflict within him is not stopping...</b>

11
00:01:08.875 --> 00:01:09.958
<b>O Madhava, </b>

12
00:01:09.958 --> 00:01:14.041
<b>it is true that those people who are</b>
<b>opposing me in the war </b>

13
00:01:14.041 --> 00:01:18.333
<b>are aggressors,</b>
<b>but won't there be sin in killing them?</b>

14
00:01:18.333 --> 00:01:21.500
<b>What sin in killing aggressors, Arjuna?</b>

15
00:01:21.500 --> 00:01:23.750
<b>Isn't it the duty of a Kshatriya</b>

16
00:01:23.750 --> 00:01:25.625
<b>to fight against aggressors,</b>

17
00:01:25.625 --> 00:01:26.958
<b>defeat them,</b>

18
00:01:26.958 --> 00:01:28.875
<b>protect his people,</b>

19
00:01:28.875 --> 00:01:31.041
<b>and safeguard dharma?</b>

20
00:01:31.041 --> 00:01:32.416
<b>This is true,</b>

21
00:01:32.416 --> 00:01:35.291
<b>but they are not just aggressors,</b>

22
00:01:35.291 --> 00:01:36.333
<b>they are my own,</b>

23
00:01:36.333 --> 00:01:37.666
<b>my kin.</b>

24
00:01:37.666 --> 00:01:41.375
<b>The sin of killing family members</b>
<b>will surely be incurred.</b>

25
00:01:41.375 --> 00:01:44.250
<b>And the sin of turning away from one's duty? </b>

26
00:01:44.250 --> 00:01:48.125
<b>Do you not fear that, Arjuna?</b>

27
00:01:48.125 --> 00:01:50.291
<b>Kshatriya dharma and duty?</b>

28
00:01:50.291 --> 00:01:53.333
<b>What is the benefit of this when our</b>
<b>own will not remain,</b>

29
00:01:53.333 --> 00:01:55.333
<b>the clan itself will be destroyed.</b>

30
00:01:55.333 --> 00:01:59.500
<b>We will be forever miserable and</b>
<b>unhappy after killing them.</b>

31
00:01:59.500 --> 00:02:00.875
<b>What is the benefit of this?</b>

32
00:02:00.875 --> 00:02:03.333
<b>What is the benefit, Madhava?</b>

33
00:02:03.333 --> 00:02:08.250
<b>Somewhere, Arjuna is also prodding Krishna</b>
<b>in his internal conflict,</b>

34
00:02:08.250 --> 00:02:10.041
<b>saying that you yourself are Madhava,</b>

35
00:02:10.041 --> 00:02:11.875
<b>the lord of Goddess Lakshmi, </b>

36
00:02:11.875 --> 00:02:13.791
<b>the lord of wealth and prosperity.</b>

37
00:02:13.791 --> 00:02:17.416
<b>Why are you pushing me</b>
<b>towards this misfortune?</b>

38
00:02:17.416 --> 00:02:19.583
<b>But you also know that</b>

39
00:02:19.583 --> 00:02:24.250
<b>not a single word has come out of</b>
<b>Krishna's mouth in response so far... </b>

40
00:02:24.250 --> 00:02:29.708
<b>In his anguish, within his own mind, and </b>
<b>even more intensely with Krishna, Arjuna keeps </b>

41
00:02:29.708 --> 00:02:33.083
<b>presenting one argument</b>
<b>after another to himself.</b>

42
00:02:33.791 --> 00:02:37.916


43
00:02:37.916 --> 00:02:44.250
<b>Do not judge Arjuna's entire personality based</b>
<b>on his current mental state. </b>

44
00:02:44.250 --> 00:02:51.000
<b>This situation is like a small</b>
<b>pebble stuck in a shoe.</b>

45
00:02:51.000 --> 00:02:53.583
<b>It will be resolved.</b>

46
00:02:53.583 --> 00:02:58.958
<b>And it is natural for the mind</b>
<b>to be filled with doubts</b>

47
00:02:58.958 --> 00:03:03.375
<b>and experience inner turmoil</b>
<b>like this from time to time.</b>

48
00:03:03.375 --> 00:03:06.500
<b>If you want to learn a lesson</b>
<b>for your personal life,</b>

49
00:03:06.500 --> 00:03:09.500
<b>take this:</b>

50
00:03:09.500 --> 00:03:11.166
<b>How easy it</b>

51
00:03:11.166 --> 00:03:16.375
<b>would be to say that I have no fault in this, </b>

52
00:03:16.375 --> 00:03:18.666
<b>the fault is of the Kauravas,</b>

53
00:03:18.666 --> 00:03:20.041
<b>they will suffer,</b>

54
00:03:20.041 --> 00:03:23.458
<b>and whoever stands with them will suffer.</b>

55
00:03:23.458 --> 00:03:28.958
<b>What is it to me? </b>

56
00:03:28.958 --> 00:03:30.625
<b>But</b>

57
00:03:30.625 --> 00:03:35.791
<b>Arjuna is not doing so out of ego or anger.</b>

58
00:03:35.791 --> 00:03:37.750
<b>He is contemplating.</b>

59
00:03:37.750 --> 00:03:44.958
<b>He is taking full responsibility for the situation</b>
<b>that will arise after the war as well.</b>

60
00:03:44.958 --> 00:03:46.458
<b>Your life too,</b>

61
00:03:46.458 --> 00:03:47.541
<b>its goodness,</b>

62
00:03:47.541 --> 00:03:48.666
<b> its unpleasantness,</b>

63
00:03:48.666 --> 00:03:52.625
<b>its joys, its sorrows, everything.</b>

64
00:03:52.625 --> 00:03:55.875
<b>Everything is your responsibility.</b>

65
00:03:55.875 --> 00:03:58.541
<b>If something bad happens unexpectedly,</b>

66
00:03:58.541 --> 00:04:00.791
<b>it may be beyond your control,</b>

67
00:04:00.791 --> 00:04:02.083
<b>but</b>

68
00:04:02.083 --> 00:04:04.625
<b>the effort to emerge from that difficult time,</b>

69
00:04:04.625 --> 00:04:06.666
<b>to rise after falling,</b>

70
00:04:06.666 --> 00:04:11.916
<b>to step from sorrow towards happiness. </b>

71
00:04:11.916 --> 00:04:16.916
<b>You will have to make that effort, right?</b>

72
00:04:16.916 --> 00:04:19.750
<b>The full responsibility of your life</b>

73
00:04:19.750 --> 00:04:21.333
<b>is yours alone, right?</b>

74
00:04:21.333 --> 00:04:24.166
<b>not someone else's.</b>

75
00:04:24.166 --> 00:04:26.375
<b>This is the truth,</b>

76
00:04:26.375 --> 00:04:29.583
<b>the sooner you realize it,</b>

77
00:04:29.583 --> 00:04:33.083
<b>the sooner you will find all the answers</b>
<b>within your mind.</b>

78
00:04:33.583 --> 00:04:37.750


79
00:04:37.750 --> 00:04:40.500
<b>If Arjuna does not take up arms,</b>

80
00:04:40.500 --> 00:04:42.833
<b>then someone else will,</b>

81
00:04:42.833 --> 00:04:44.791
<b>either from the Kauravas</b>

82
00:04:44.791 --> 00:04:47.000
<b>or the Pandavas.</b>

83
00:04:47.000 --> 00:04:51.833
<b>Those destined to die will perish,</b>

84
00:04:51.833 --> 00:04:55.041
<b>as war is the final stage.</b>

85
00:04:55.041 --> 00:04:55.875
<b>Infact,</b>

86
00:04:55.875 --> 00:04:58.333
<b>by tying his hands in war,</b>

87
00:04:58.333 --> 00:05:02.125
<b>Arjuna will only weaken</b>
<b>the side of righteousness</b>

88
00:05:02.125 --> 00:05:05.583
<b>and empower the unrighteous.</b>

89
00:05:05.583 --> 00:05:08.458
<b>This dilemma is natural,</b>

90
00:05:08.458 --> 00:05:09.208
<b>but</b>

91
00:05:09.208 --> 00:05:12.583
<b>arms must be taken up.</b>

92
00:05:12.583 --> 00:05:14.500
<b>Well but you?</b>

93
00:05:14.500 --> 00:05:16.166
<b>Your life situation</b>

94
00:05:16.166 --> 00:05:18.666
<b>or family situation </b>

95
00:05:18.666 --> 00:05:22.333
<b>may not be as dire as this war, right?</b>

96
00:05:22.333 --> 00:05:27.541
<b>If a young one in the family</b>
<b>is inclined towards sin,</b>

97
00:05:27.541 --> 00:05:31.333
<b>will you simply watch in silence?</b>

98
00:05:31.333 --> 00:05:36.583
<b>If a peer or an elder has unrighteous intentions</b>

99
00:05:36.583 --> 00:05:40.166
<b>or engaged in unrighteous acts,</b>

100
00:05:40.166 --> 00:05:43.208
<b>then in the fear of damaging your relationship,</b>

101
00:05:43.208 --> 00:05:50.125
<b>will you seal your lips? and not voice yourself?</b>

102
00:05:50.125 --> 00:05:52.541
<b>A gardener</b>

103
00:05:52.541 --> 00:05:56.416
<b>puts in his best efforts,</b>

104
00:05:56.416 --> 00:06:03.000
<b>watering each plant and flower</b>
<b>with his hard work and sweat.</b>

105
00:06:03.000 --> 00:06:04.416
<b>But</b>

106
00:06:04.416 --> 00:06:07.541
<b>sometimes, if a pest infests a branch,</b>

107
00:06:07.541 --> 00:06:10.583
<b>treatment becomes necessary.</b>

108
00:06:10.583 --> 00:06:14.541
<b>Even if a beautiful flower blooms on that branch,</b>

109
00:06:14.541 --> 00:06:17.333
<b>it may need to be cut off.</b>

110
00:06:17.333 --> 00:06:24.541
<b>It's not that the gardener doesn't love</b>
<b>this plant or this flower,</b>

111
00:06:24.541 --> 00:06:27.875
<b>as he has nurtured it too.</b>

112
00:06:27.875 --> 00:06:28.916
<b>But </b>

113
00:06:28.916 --> 00:06:31.625
<b>if one branch remains unhealthy,</b>

114
00:06:31.625 --> 00:06:34.375
<b>the entire plant will become unhealthy,</b>

115
00:06:34.375 --> 00:06:40.041
<b>and the same pest can spoil the entire garden.</b>

116
00:06:40.041 --> 00:06:41.791
<b>Similarly,</b>

117
00:06:41.791 --> 00:06:44.833
<b>in the garden of your family,</b>

118
00:06:44.833 --> 00:06:47.958
<b>there are various colorful flowers and plants,</b>

119
00:06:47.958 --> 00:06:48.875
<b>some big </b>

120
00:06:48.875 --> 00:06:50.375
<b>and some small.</b>

121
00:06:50.375 --> 00:06:53.208
<b>If you observe something</b>
<b>going wrong somewhere,</b>

122
00:06:53.208 --> 00:06:56.000
<b>it is necessary to draw attention to it</b>

123
00:06:56.000 --> 00:06:58.541
<b>and provide timely treatment.</b>

124
00:06:58.541 --> 00:07:07.083
<b>It is essential to guide and restrain</b>
<b>any unrighteous tendency.</b>

125
00:07:07.083 --> 00:07:08.750
<b>Otherwise,</b>

126
00:07:08.750 --> 00:07:12.333
<b>sin is like a wild creeper;</b>

127
00:07:12.333 --> 00:07:16.041
<b>it won't take long to entangle others.</b>

128
00:07:16.583 --> 00:07:20.583


129
00:07:20.583 --> 00:07:23.041
<b>In the context of professional life,</b>

130
00:07:23.041 --> 00:07:25.958
<b>there is certainly a lesson to be learned here.</b>

131
00:07:25.958 --> 00:07:30.000
<b>Arjuna is not taking up arms in excitement;</b>

132
00:07:30.000 --> 00:07:31.458
<b>he is thinking,</b>

133
00:07:31.458 --> 00:07:33.041
<b>understanding,</b>

134
00:07:33.041 --> 00:07:34.541
<b>considering the immediate consequences</b>

135
00:07:34.541 --> 00:07:37.583
<b>and, even more importantly,</b>

136
00:07:37.583 --> 00:07:39.083
<b>the long-term consequences.</b>

137
00:07:39.083 --> 00:07:40.833
<b>He is thinking about</b>

138
00:07:40.833 --> 00:07:45.500
<b>the impact on every person involved in the war,</b>

139
00:07:45.500 --> 00:07:48.750
<b>both those he likes </b>

140
00:07:48.750 --> 00:07:52.916
<b>and those he dislikes.</b>

141
00:07:52.916 --> 00:07:54.750
<b>in a true leader,</b>

142
00:07:54.750 --> 00:07:57.291
<b>someone who leads an organization,</b>

143
00:07:57.291 --> 00:07:59.666
<b>his quality is essential.</b>

144
00:07:59.666 --> 00:08:04.125
<b>It is your responsibility to think and reflect,</b>

145
00:08:04.125 --> 00:08:05.583
<b>to consider the long-term,</b>

146
00:08:05.583 --> 00:08:09.250
<b>and to understand the</b>
<b>impact on all your colleagues,</b>

147
00:08:09.250 --> 00:08:13.750
<b>even those with whom you disagree.</b>

148
00:08:13.750 --> 00:08:15.125
<b>It's not that</b>

149
00:08:15.125 --> 00:08:17.375
<b>the people you dislike</b>

150
00:08:17.375 --> 00:08:19.708
<b>are bad.</b>

151
00:08:19.708 --> 00:08:23.666
<b>A good leader must think about them too.</b>

152
00:08:23.666 --> 00:08:25.125
<b>A musician,</b>

153
00:08:25.125 --> 00:08:29.416
<b>by weaving together various sounds and notes</b>
<b>from different instruments,</b>

154
00:08:29.416 --> 00:08:33.125
<b>creates a captivating song.</b>

155
00:08:33.125 --> 00:08:35.583
<b>Similarly, a leader,</b>

156
00:08:35.583 --> 00:08:41.375
<b>despite agreements and disagreements</b>
<b>among diverse people, </b>

157
00:08:41.375 --> 00:08:42.666
<b>assigns them to the right places,</b>

158
00:08:42.666 --> 00:08:47.291
<b>balances them, and leads</b>
<b>the organization to success.</b>

